# Four independent spatial pendulums hanging from a common fixed base --
# the maximally parallel topology: every body's parent is the base, so the
# joint-space inertia matrix is diagonal (Featherstone's branch-induced
# sparsity, CRBA.pdf slide 11, second pattern) and the CRBA ancestor walk
# terminates immediately for every body. Axes alternate x and y and the
# rods hang in -z, so all three dimensions participate.

gravity 0 0 -9.81

body                    # 0
parent -1
joint revolute x
tree 1 0 0
mass 1
cg 0 0 -0.5
inertia 0.09 0.09 0.01 0 0 0
fext 1

body                    # 1
parent -1
joint revolute y
tree -1 0 0
mass 2
cg 0 0 -0.4
inertia 0.12 0.12 0.02 0 0 0

body                    # 2
parent -1
joint revolute x
tree 0 1 0
mass 0.5
cg 0 0.05 -0.6
inertia 0.06 0.06 0.005 0 0 0

body                    # 3
parent -1
joint revolute y
tree 0 -1 0.2
mass 1.5
cg 0.05 0 -0.45
inertia 0.1 0.11 0.02 0 0 0
fext 1
